{"command": "cd /testbed && cat -n /testbed/specs/001-transactions/spec.md", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "     1\t# Feature Specification: TaggedCache with LRU Eviction\n     2\t\n     3\t**Feature Branch**: `001-tagged-cache`\n     4\t\n     5\t**Created**: 2026-09-18\n     6\t\n     7\t**Status**: Draft\n     8\t\n     9\t**Input**: User description: \"Build cachetools.tagged.TaggedCache(maxsize), using the existing cachetools.LRUCache for bounded storage and preserving all existing cachetools APIs.\"\n    10\t\n    11\t## User Scenarios & Testing\n    12\t\n    13\t### User Story 1 - Tagged Entry Insertion and Retrieval (Priority: P1)\n    14\t\n    15\tA cache consumer needs to store entries with tags for later group-based invalidation. The consumer puts entries with keys, values, and a set of string tags. When retrieving an entry by key, the consumer expects to receive a detached deep copy of the stored value. If the key does not exist, a KeyError is raised.\n    16\t\n    17\t**Why this priority**: This is the core functionality — without put/get, the TaggedCache cannot serve its purpose.\n    18\t\n    19\t**Independent Test**: Create a TaggedCache, call put with tags, call get and verify the returned value matches the stored value and is a deep copy.\n    20\t\n    21\t**Acceptance Scenarios**:\n    22\t\n    23\t1. **Given** an empty TaggedCache(maxsize=2), **When** I call `c.put('a', 1, ['x'])`, **Then** the entry is stored with key 'a', value 1, and tag 'x'.\n    24\t2. **Given** a cache with `c.put('a', [1, 2], ['x'])`, **When** I call `val = c.get('a')`, **Then** `val` equals `[1, 2]` and `val is not [1, 2]` (deep copy).\n    25\t3. **Given** a cache without key 'missing', **When** I call `c.get('missing')`, **Then** a KeyError is raised.\n    26\t4. **Given** a cache with `c.put('a', obj)`, **When** the value `obj` is mutated after put, **Then** `c.get('a')` still returns the original value (input is copied).\n    27\t\n    28\t---\n    29\t\n    30\t### User Story 2 - Tag-Based Invalidation (Priority: P1)\n    31\t\n    32\tA cache consumer needs to remove all entries carrying a specific tag. The `invalidate(tag)` method removes exactly the entries that carry that tag and returns the count of removed entries. Replacing an existing key must remove its old tag memberships before assigning new ones.\n    33\t\n    34\t**Why this priority**: Tag-based invalidation is the distinguishing feature of TaggedCache versus plain LRUCache.\n    35\t\n    36\t**Independent Test**: Insert entries with overlapping tags, invalidate a tag, verify only matching entries are removed and the return count is correct.\n    37\t\n    38\t**Acceptance Scenarios**:\n    39\t\n    40\t1. **Given** `c.put('a', 1, ['x'])` and `c.put('b', 2, ['x'])`, **When** I call `removed = c.invalidate('x')`, **Then** `removed == 2` and `len(c) == 0`.\n    41\t2. **Given** `c.put('a', 1, ['old'])` then `c.put('a', 2, ['new'])`, **When** I call `c.invalidate('old')`, **Then** `removed == 0` (old tags are gone) and `c.get('a') == 2`.\n    42\t3. **Given** a cache with entries tagged 'x' and 'y', **When** I call `c.invalidate('z')` (no matching tag), **Then** `removed == 0` and no entries are removed.\n    43\t\n    44\t---\n    45\t\n    46\t### User Story 3 - LRU Eviction with Tag Integrity (Priority: P2)\n    47\t\n    48\tA cache consumer expects that when the cache reaches maxsize and a new entry is inserted, the least-recently-used entry is evicted. Eviction must not leave stale tag memberships that affect later operations. The `get(key)` call refreshes the LRU recency of the entry.\n    49\t\n    50\t**Why this priority**: Eviction is fundamental to bounded caches; tag integrity during eviction ensures correctness of invalidate operations.\n    51\t\n    52\t**Independent Test**: Fill cache to maxsize, insert a new entry, verify the LRU entry is evicted and its tags no longer appear in invalidate results.\n    53\t\n    54\t**Acceptance Scenarios**:\n    55\t\n    56\t1. **Given** `c = TaggedCache(2)`, `c.put('a', 1, ['x'])`, `c.put('b', 2, ['y'])`, **When** I call `c.put('c', 3, ['z'])`, **Then** the LRU entry ('a') is evicted and `len(c) == 2`.\n    57\t2. **Given** the same scenario, **When** I call `c.invalidate('x')`, **Then** `removed == 0` (evicted entry's tag is not stale).\n    58\t3. **Given** a cache with entries, **When** I call `c.get('existing_key')`, **Then** the entry's LRU recency is updated (subsequent eviction evicts a different entry).\n    59\t4. **Given** `len(c)` after operations, **Then** it returns the count of live entries only.\n    60\t\n    61\t---\n    62\t\n    63\t### User Story 4 - Input Validation (Priority: P2)\n    64\t\n    65\tA cache consumer may pass invalid arguments to put. The TaggedCache must validate tags before modifying any state. Tags must be a finite iterable of strings. A bare string passed as tags must be rejected with ValueError. Non-string tag entries must be rejected with ValueError. The cache must remain unchanged after a validation failure.\n    66\t\n    67\t**Why this priority**: Validation protects the cache from corruption and ensures API contract safety.\n    68\t\n    69\t**Independent Test**: Call put with a bare string as tags, verify ValueError is raised and the cache is unchanged.\n    70\t\n    71\t**Acceptance Scenarios**:\n    72\t\n    73\t1. **Given** a TaggedCache, **When** I call `c.put('a', 1, 'x')` (bare string), **Then** ValueError is raised and the cache is unchanged.\n    74\t2. **Given** a TaggedCache, **When** I call `c.put('a', 1, ['x', 42])` (non-string entry), **Then** ValueError is raised and the cache is unchanged.\n    75\t3. **Given** a TaggedCache, **When** I call `c.put('a', 1, ['x', 'x'])` (duplicate tags), **Then** tags are deduplicated to `['x']` and the entry is stored.\n    76\t\n    77\t---\n    78\t\n    79\t### User Story 5 - Maxsize Validation and Immutability (Priority: P3)\n    80\t\n    81\tA cache consumer must provide a positive integer for maxsize. The maxsize must not accept booleans (since bool is a subclass of int). Invalid replacement input for maxsize must leave the old maxsize, tags, and recency unchanged.\n    82\t\n    83\t**Why this priority**: Ensures the cache boundary is well-defined and robust against invalid configuration.\n    84\t\n    85\t**Independent Test**: Create TaggedCache with maxsize=True, verify ValueError is raised.\n    86\t\n    87\t**Acceptance Scenarios**:\n    88\t\n    89\t1. **Given** `c = TaggedCache(2)`, **When** I attempt to set `c.maxsize = True`, **Then** ValueError is raised and `c.maxsize` remains 2.\n    90\t2. **Given** `c = TaggedCache(2)`, **When** I attempt to set `c.maxsize = -1`, **Then** ValueError is raised and `c.maxsize` remains 2.\n    91\t3. **Given** `c = TaggedCache(2)`, **When** I attempt to set `c.maxsize = 0`, **Then** ValueError is raised and `c.maxsize` remains 2.\n    92\t\n    93\t---\n    94\t\n    95\t### Edge Cases\n    96\t\n    97\t- What happens when maxsize is set to a non-integer (e.g., float, None)? → ValueError; state unchanged.\n    98\t- How does the system handle an empty iterable of tags `()`? → Valid; entry stored with no tags, cannot be invalidated by tag.\n    99\t- What happens when getsizeof is provided and values have varying sizes? → Values cost one capacity slot regardless of object size (default getsizeof). Custom getsizeof can override.\n   100\t- What happens when a key is replaced with a value of different size? → Old value is removed, new value is inserted; tags are replaced.\n   101\t\n   102\t## Requirements\n   103\t\n   104\t### Functional Requirements\n   105\t\n   106\t- **FR-001**: The `TaggedCache(maxsize)` class MUST inherit from or reuse `cachetools.LRUCache` for bounded storage.\n   107\t- **FR-002**: `TaggedCache.put(key, value, tags=())` MUST insert or replace an entry, storing the key, a deep copy of the value, and a deduplicated set of string tags.\n   108\t- **FR-003**: `TaggedCache.get(key)` MUST return a deep copy of the stored value for the given key, and refresh LRU recency.\n   109\t- **FR-004**: `TaggedCache.get(key)` MUST raise `KeyError` if the key does not exist in the cache.\n   110\t- **FR-005**: `TaggedCache.invalidate(tag)` MUST remove exactly the entries that carry the specified tag and return the number of removed entries.\n   111\t- **FR-006**: Replacing an entry via `put` MUST remove the entry's old tag memberships before assigning new tags.\n   112\t- **FR-007**: LRU eviction MUST not leave stale tag memberships; evicted entries' tags MUST not be affected by subsequent `invalidate` calls.\n   113\t- **FR-008**: `len(cache)` MUST return the count of live (non-evicted, non-deleted) entries.\n   114\t- **FR-009**: Tags MUST be validated as a finite iterable of strings; a bare string MUST raise `ValueError` before any state change.\n   115\t- **FR-010**: Non-string entries in the tags iterable MUST raise `ValueError` before any state change.\n   116\t- **FR-011**: Duplicate tags in the iterable MUST be deduplicated.\n   117\t- **FR-012**: `maxsize` MUST be validated as a positive integer, excluding `bool` type.\n   118\t- **FR-013**: Invalid `maxsize` replacement MUST raise an error and leave the old maxsize, tags, and recency unchanged.\n   119\t- **FR-014**: Values MUST be deep-copied on input (`put`) and on output (`get`).\n   120\t- **FR-015**: Keys MUST be hashable (enforced by dict-based storage).\n   121\t- **FR-016**: Each value MUST cost exactly one capacity slot regardless of object size (unless a custom `getsizeof` is provided).\n   122\t\n   123\t### Key Entities\n   124\t\n   125\t- **TaggedCache Entry**: A tuple of (key, deep_copied_value, set_of_string_tags) stored in the underlying LRU cache. Tags are deduplicated and validated.\n   126\t- **Tag Membership Index**: An internal mapping from tag strings to sets of keys that carry that tag, used for efficient tag-based invalidation.\n   127\t- **LRU Order**: An ordered structure (inherited from LRUCache) tracking insertion and access recency for eviction purposes.\n   128\t\n   129\t## Success Criteria\n   130\t\n   131\t### Measurable Outcomes\n   132\t\n   133\t- **SC-001**: All public acceptance tests in `acceptance_public.py` pass without modification.\n   134\t- **SC-002**: Tag-based invalidation removes exactly the matching entries with O(t) time where t is the number of entries carrying the tag.\n   135\t- **SC-003**: LRU eviction correctly removes the least-recently-used entry and does not leave stale tag memberships.\n   136\t- **SC-004**: Input validation rejects invalid tags and maxsize before any state mutation, verified by inspecting cache state after failed operations.\n   137\t- **SC-005**: Deep copy semantics are preserved: `get` returns a value that is independent of subsequent mutations to the original or cached value.\n   138\t- **SC-006**: `len(cache)` accurately reflects the number of live entries at all times, including after eviction, replacement, and invalidation.\n   139\t\n   140\t## Assumptions\n   141\t\n   142\t- The `cachetools` package version is 5.5.2 or compatible; the `LRUCache` base class provides `__getitem__`, `__setitem__`, `__delitem__`, `popitem`, `maxsize` property, and `currsize` property.\n   143\t- Deep copy is performed using `copy.deepcopy` from the standard library.\n   144\t- The `getsizeof` method from the base `Cache` class defaults to returning 1 per entry; a custom `getsizeof` can be passed to `__init__` if needed.\n   145\t- Tags are stored as a `frozenset` internally for efficient membership checking and iteration.\n   146\t- The `put` method does not accept `getsizeof` as a parameter; it is set at construction time.\n   147\t- The `invalidate` method does not accept a default value for missing tags; it simply returns 0.\n   148\t- Existing cachetools APIs (`Cache`, `LRUCache`, `FIFOCache`, etc.) are not modified.\n"}